# What the web CI image's build may see of the checkout.
#
# It is an allowlist, and a narrow one: the context sent to the builder is the
# handful of scripts this image installs rather than the whole checkout, so
# nothing else a commit touches is uploaded or busts a layer.
#
# There is a second reason this file exists, and it is the one that would
# otherwise break the build outright. BuildKit reads the ignore file named
# after the Dockerfile in preference to the root .dockerignore, and this
# workspace has a root .dockerignore: an allowlist written for the images under
# deployments/, which ignores everything and re-includes the Rust and web
# workspaces those builds read. A CI image reads none of that and copies the
# devcontainer's install scripts instead, so under that allowlist every COPY
# below would fail with the source not found.
#
# The paths are the COPY sources of web.Dockerfile. The image pipeline's path
# filter lists more than these: it names every file the image is built from,
# which includes the files that decide the build command and never reach the
# image.

*
!/.devcontainer/languages/node
!/.devcontainer/system/browser-deps.sh
!/.devcontainer/tools/browsers.sh
!/.devcontainer/tools/kubectl.sh
!/.devcontainer/tools/uv.sh
